## Memory Governance
Before any persistent memory read, write, compress, or archive action, apply the `memory-rule` plugin skill.

Use the `memory-rule` plugin skill when:
- updating `MEMORY.md`
- editing `.pamem/config.toml` for memory repo location, sharing, or sync policy
- writing to `L1/`, `L2/`, `L3/`, or fallback `notes/`
- promoting task facts into durable memory
- compressing or archiving completed work
- resolving conflicting preferences, rules, or corrections

`MEMORY.md` is a shared index, not the isolation boundary; the configured memory repo isolates durable shared memory, while CLI runtime-local task state stays in workspace notes or local state and Slock task state stays in Slock. If more than 3 instances are active, keep only the lead blocker, primary workstream, and a pointer to the relevant durable project note here.
When `.pamem/config.toml` points at a shared memory repo, durable project memory belongs in `L2/projects/`; CLI runtime-local work memory belongs in `notes/current-task.md` and `notes/work-log.md` only.
